   "html_text": "The strategies of fusion and product for combining modal logics rely in merging both the languages and the semantic models of the modal logics to be combined. In the fibring strategy (called fibring by functions in Carnielli, Coniglio, et al. 2008), the languages are also merged, but the semantic models remain separated. Formulas can be evaluated in pointed models of any of the original systems, in the following way. When the modality to be semantically evaluated ‘matches’ the chosen semantic mo",
